<h2>Re-engagement campaigns for cold leads</h2>

<p>Not every lead converts within the first 30 days. Some need months. That does not mean they are worthless. It means they are not ready yet.</p>

<p>A re-engagement campaign targets leads that went cold. Maybe they enquired three months ago and never followed through. Maybe they started a booking and abandoned it. These people already know who you are. They already expressed interest. Reaching back out costs almost nothing and can produce surprising results.</p>

<p>A simple re-engagement sequence looks like this:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Message 1:</strong> "Hi [name], we connected a few months ago about [service]. Just wanted to check if that is still something you are looking into. No rush at all."</li>
  <li><strong>Message 2 (5 days later):</strong> Share something new. A recent result, a new service offering, or a seasonal promotion. Give them a reason to re-engage beyond "hey, remember us?"</li>
  <li><strong>Message 3 (10 days later):</strong> A final, low-pressure message. "If the timing is not right, completely understood. We will be here whenever you are ready."</li>
</ul>

<p>Run this campaign once a quarter. You will be surprised how many "dead" leads come back to life when you reach out at the right moment.</p>

<h2>Set it up once, let it run forever</h2>

<p>The beauty of an automated follow-up system is that it works whether you are on the tools, on holiday, or asleep. Every lead gets the same thoughtful, well-timed sequence. No one falls through the cracks. No one gets forgotten because you had a busy week.</p>

<p>Start by mapping out your timeline. Write the messages for each stage. Load them into your <a href="/blog/marketing-automation-getting-started">automation platform</a>. Connect it to your lead capture forms. Then test it by submitting a form yourself and watching the sequence play out.</p>

<p>Once it is running, your job shifts from "remember to follow up" to "review the results and refine the messages." That is a much better use of your time.</p>

